WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.650
Due to a multiple-vehicle pileup accident, traffic on Atmospheric Route 8...

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.930
is backed up for over 600,000 kilometers.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:08.780
Passage is expected to take over 80 hours.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.050
In other news, Route 14's reopening will take place 2 hours ahead of schedule...

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:17.530
First Natural Satellite, the Moon

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:18.930
Despite getting the chance...

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:19.250
to welcome a small-statured heroine...

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:21.330
Former Plato Crater
to welcome a small-statured heroine...

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:21.340
I'm deeply ashamed to say we're unable to have...
Former Plato Crater

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:21.380
I'm deeply ashamed to say we're unable to have...

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.690
Lunar Tokyo: The Imperial City

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.020
the townspeople throw even a welcoming parade.

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:27.300
Lunar Tokyo: The Imperial City

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.220
The darkness throughout the city is not a blackout, either.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.620
Much like the Earth, everyone has evacuated en masse...

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.740
So now, even the imperial city, Lunar Tokyo, is a ghost town.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.760
Ah, it's about time for Earthrise.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:45.490
It'll be beautiful.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.140
We cannot yet grant landing permission to
Paymaster Captain with the 15th Grand Fleet.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:53.460
Oh dear, my mistake...

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.210
that was <i>Douze-Mille</i>.

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:56.640
Ultra-Large-Scale Ether-Accelerated Assault Weapon, <i>Douze-Mille</i>

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.720
Still, with a weapon this huge...

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.430
our victory is practically assured.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.450
Though, of course...

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:02.460
Ultra-Large-Scale Ether-Accelerated Assault Weapon, <i>Douze-Mille</i>

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.520
the beautiful view of Earth is obscured by its shadow...

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:08.780
The Earth?!

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:13.640
I want to go there, it's where you were born!

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.150
Plus, the Earth is...

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:19.230
It looks like our next stop is Jupiter. We don't get much vacation time, either.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:20.810
Aww!

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.470
But I'm sure we'll get another chance, right?

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.800
The metropolitan governor will go on back ahead.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.220
After this, he is scheduled to return to the evacuation ship. Over.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:38.110
She will be handed over to the Privy Staff Council's attached escort.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.700
You can go ahead and call off the traffic suspension.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.000
Don't touch my hair!

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.510
Final Episode:
The Story of Your Life

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.510
The Nest Hole of the space monsters...

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:52.570
that have kept mankind trapped within the Sol System for thousands of years...

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.690
we call it the Red Milky Way...

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.100
In the past 6 months, it's vanished.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.640
This is the body that they pooled together to form.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.100
However, 48 hours ago...

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.530
it suddenly vanished from the former Jupiter 2's orbit.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.200
Its whereabouts after that are unknown.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.960
In the end, #7 disappeared in front of us without giving us any protection.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.770
Why is #7, the defense system of the Sol System...

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.460
taking on a humanoid shape?

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.310
There's no clear answer.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:37.990
Perhaps this is reminiscent of ancient civilizations that molded gods in their own image?

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:38.800
Or perhaps...

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.890
Forget about #7 already.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.140
#7 has her own way of living.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.150
I'm glad you could make it.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:52.940
Amazing, for such a tiny body to move a planet...

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:56.570
You must be tired from the long trip. Please, have a seat.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:00.570
Do you have any cocoa?

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.070
Mind your manners, Lal'C Mellk Mal.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.160
The operation is starting soon.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.870
Aren't any of you going to evacuate?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.130
Mover of planets...

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:19.600
Must mankind go this far in order to survive?

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.160
Sacrificing the Earth is the only way to save mankind.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:29.850
Even if humanity itself evolves into fluctuating gravity wells in order to stay alive?

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.100
Let whoever survives be the judge of that.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:34.950
Mm-hmm...

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.480
We are not gods, after all.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.000
Thank you. I just wanted to meet and confirm it directly, face-to-face.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.920
The key to <i>Douze-Mille</i> is best off in your hands.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:02.580
Even with the realization that the Red Milky Way is gone for good...

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:04.910
humanity's still stuck cowering in fear.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:10.970
And after legendary hidden ruins were finally discovered, too...

00:04:12.490 --> 00:04:16.530
Buster Machine Public Corporation Moon Arsenal, Dock 1

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.290
When you reach your expiration...

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:29.890
do you get the impression that you've been betrayed by the Buster Machines?

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.090
No, sir.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:36.570
Their existence has always been on a level far from that of humans, an eternal one.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.550
The Topless are no more than batteries to them, to be used up and tossed out.

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:47.810
Fighting with no regard for death is something that should be left only to Buster Machines.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.640
Well, I'll try to tell her, but...

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.830
I saw in the papers that she was coming to Tokyo.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.830
So I was waiting at the gate to catch her on the way in...

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:00.090
when an MP comes up and... Now I've got this black eye.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:04.370
A mere mechanic like me cannot even talk to her.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.170
Of course not.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.290
On Mars, there was an assassination attempt by an opposing faction.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.300
Even I'm not allowed to meet with her after that.

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.050
C'mon, Onee-sama!

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:19.880
I'll pass on taking pictures. My hairstyle's all weird right now...

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.340
Okay, Onee-sama, you've got to smile for the camera!

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.840
CUCKOO!

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.100
Okay, everyone, smile for the camera.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.660
Isn't this the first time everyone's gathered together like this?

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.550
In the last hundred years or so, yeah.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.870
Did you reserve this whole stadium, Miss Lal'C?

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:45.490
Well, nobody's left in Tokyo, and there's no swearing-in ceremony this year, either.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.040
And, well, this is kinda like a graduation ceremony.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.040
I wanted to get a shot together with everyone now...

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:00.790
Sorry, but would you mind leaving this seat empty?

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:04.590
Ah, for Roy... You two got along well, didn't you?

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:06.510
He was one of the good ones.

00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:09.890
So were Nhan, Gurka, and Pasika.

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.900
Okay, one more.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.230
Casio said not to push yourself too hard.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:28.140
Yeah, you'll never get any boys with an expression like that.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.870
If we lose, there won't be anything to get.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:32.750
Ever the "Curve Wrecker," aren't you?

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.670
Don't tell me you've got a fever?

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:41.650
I'm the mover of planets.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.100
Two Months Ago

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:47.980
Mars, Marineris

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.170
C'mon, knock it off.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.150
Quit it... Could you stop?!

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.270
Cut it out, you dumb dog!

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.740
Well, isn't this a surprise!

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.580
Miss Lal'C, right?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:57.540
They're supposedly constructing a hundred thousand more of those things on Mars.

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:00.960
Even so, 70% are up in orbit on standby.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.920
Cocoa... Did Nono like it too?

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:07.190
She loved Japanese cuisine...

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:10.110
because Nono-Riri was a traditional Japanese girl, she said.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.920
Do you know who that is?

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:16.180
All I know is, she was the heroine who saved the Sol System long, long ago.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.760
I wonder if it was the same for her...

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.650
being built long, long ago to protect the Sol System.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:28.450
When I found her, she had lost most of her memories...

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:33.400
The prison of a life lasting thousands, or even tens of thousands of years...

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:38.600
I could never even begin to understand how horrible that might have been.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.350
But, what part of the Sol System was she built to protect?

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:46.760
When you think about that, don't you think you can almost get a grasp on...

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:50.840
why she was given a human shape and a human heart?

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.710
I wanted to let her meet Nono-Riri.

00:08:55.210 --> 00:09:00.540
Assuming that, as Nono claimed, Nono-Riri really was a normal girl...

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.260
I suppose she would need a friend.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:08.650
I guess heroes are always isolated.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:12.260
Even before, there was a girl who chose a path of solitude...

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.380
in order to protect everyone.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:20.150
I think that fact kept her going.

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.640
She had never met Nono-Riri before, either.

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:29.100
So she must have been glad to have met you, I'm sure.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:42.980
We will be returning to level 3 security at 17 o'clock. Over.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.520
Ether-focusing wave detected.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:59.260
2 minutes since P-wave arrival, 15 seconds since S-wave transition!

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:02.040
Warp out of Exelio fluctuating gravity well confirmed!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.810
Being dragged into this battle as a soldier-in-training...

00:10:04.810 --> 00:10:07.080
just 6 months after joining the army, that's some luck.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:09.860
Space Force Joint Staff Fleet (2nd Grand Fleet)

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:11.430
It's closer than we calculated.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.100
But we must have it knocked down...

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:14.310
Flagship <i>Basile</i>
But we must have it knocked down...

00:10:14.310 --> 00:10:14.350
into the black hole with <i>Douze-Mille</i> at any cost.

00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:17.190
Same Fleet, Chief of Staff

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:17.210
into the black hole with <i>Douze-Mille</i> at any cost.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:17.560
Same Fleet, Commander-in-Chief

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:18.720
As per the plan...

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:20.320
the entire fleet will create a diversion.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:24.320
We'd like to buy the mover of planets at least a little time.

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:26.720
The Fraternity's Buster Machines are heading in.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:28.950
Gravitational quake due to warp out will reach us in 11 seconds.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.140
Even though they're barely older than my daughter...

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:32.380
All ships, prepare ether absorbers.

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:36.530
An Exotic Maneuver-weakening phenomenon...

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.340
occurs near the fluctuating gravity well.

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:43.130
No acting alone. Let's stick to formation and take it on as a team.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.060
It's hard to perform under constraints...

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:47.010
They're here!

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.400
Don't let them get close to <i>Douze-Mille</i>!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.630
So it's started...

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.350
Death Anchor!

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:12.290
Southern Cross Shot!

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:13.540
Senpai!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:16.260
I know!

00:11:19.360 --> 00:11:22.260
Bastard!

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.740
Buster Blossom!

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.150
It's bigger now than it was when it first showed up, isn't it?!

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:43.690
Exelio Fluctuating Gravity Well (Third Evolution Form)

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:45.490
It's a monster...

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:55.180
It looks like acceleration course can be secured. What about the final adjustments?

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.710
I'll handle them en route.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.510
I'll just get it over with.

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:03.050
After this mission is over, you will answer to Mars military command.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.610
Who cares about that?

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:07.630
As long as the operation succeeds, what happens afterwards shouldn't matter, right?

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.440
We can't have that.

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:13.180
<i>Douze-Mille</i> is military property. I request for you to bring it back in one piece.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:15.050
Same for the pilot.

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:18.400
Thank you, Commander.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.570
But this is pretty much it.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.290
Now, <i>Dix-Neuf</i>!

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:46.560
Let's slam this planet into it and end this.

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.090
Former Third Planet in the Sol System

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:53.850
Present Ultimate Special Assault Mass Weapon for the Battle on the Mainland

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.930
Earth

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.850
<i>Douze-Mille</i>, take off!

00:13:24.410 --> 00:13:28.300
The Earth is...

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:44.150
<i>Douze-Mille</i> has embarked on a crash course with the fluctuating gravity well.

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:46.090
Our victory is assured.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.110
Are you unsatisfied with that?

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.860
I hope she's thinking the same thing...

00:13:53.380 --> 00:13:55.120
Physical canceler, full power.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:57.490
EXOTIC DRIVE!

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:14.890
The number of rotations is off the scale! And it's climbing even higher!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.510
Final acceleration! To sub-lightspeed!

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.670
Slam into it!

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:39.160
It couldn't be?!

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.800
That's the Sol System Absolute Defense System's...

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:51.880
combined form?

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:52.790
Ultra-Gigantic Humanoid Ultimate Weapon

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:55.430
Earth Imperial Space Force, Sol System Absolute Defense

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.970
DIEBUSTER!!

00:14:57.970 --> 00:14:59.510
Diebuster

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.630
Is it trying to hinder the operation?

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:18.800
But mankind lacks the power to face something so huge head-on!

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:21.870
NUMBER SEVEN!!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:29.850
<i>Douze-Mille</i>?!

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.090
Incredible!

00:15:31.090 --> 00:15:33.910
It's like a gigantic Buster Machine!

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.170
You've got a lot of nerve, showing up now! Stay out of our way!

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:43.270
This is mankind's battle!

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:47.480
A battle with everything we've got at stake!

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:53.200
We'll save mankind, even if it means abandoning the Earth!

00:15:54.580 --> 00:15:56.690
I don't care if it's right or wrong!

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.370
It's got nothing to do with you!

00:16:05.050 --> 00:16:08.500
You followed me around without asking!
You went off on your own without asking!

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.980
If we could have stayed friends forever...

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:13.960
I wouldn't have even been afraid of losing my Topless ability!

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.470
Friends...

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:19.920
The truth is, I wanted you to keep being my roommate!

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:23.800
I wanted you to come visit my home to see the skylarks!

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:25.730
I didn't want you to call me Onee-sama...

00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:28.450
but Lal'C!

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:38.340
Nono, you dumb fool!!!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:51.000
<i>Dix-Neuf</i>...

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.790
I can't hear your voice...

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.270
I see.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.930
Of all the times...

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:02.010
Lal'C's Topless ability...

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:07.720
...dumb fool...

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.810
ULTRA

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:26.880
LIGHTNING

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:32.930
KICK!!!

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:51.390
Even the killer Collider attack doesn't seem to affect it!

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:54.170
BUSTER

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:57.350
BEAM!!!

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:37.880
"The person called 'Nono-Riri'..."

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:41.140
"wasn't anybody special..."

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:45.440
"She was just an ordinary girl."

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:50.580
Lal'C...

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:51.750
Nono!

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.190
Do you understand, <i>Dix-Neuf</i>?

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:00.900
Nono's scared.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:03.170
I don't want to leave her alone out there any more!

00:19:03.170 --> 00:19:05.760
Nono! I'm on my way!

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.810
<i>Dix-Neuf</i>, Emergency Spinal Passage

00:19:17.810 --> 00:19:20.940
Casio was right, <i>Dix-Neuf</i> has...
<i>Dix-Neuf</i>, Emergency Spinal Passage

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:20.950
<i>Dix-Neuf</i>, Emergency Spinal Passage

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.620
Is this the horn in his right eye?

00:19:42.420 --> 00:19:43.970
What on Earth is he doing?

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.370
He's going to use his sealed-away power for Lal'C's sake.

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:51.600
He's going to unlock the true cockpit hidden away in his artificial brain.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:55.980
Thank you, <i>Dix-Neuf</i>.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:19:59.470
There it is!

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.400
She can't take any more!

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:20.130
The enemy is just far too big.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.180
This is the end for mankind...

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.840
Let's do it, <i>Dix-Neuf</i>!

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.780
He's taking something in?

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.060
Something that was taken away millennia ago... a degeneracy generator!

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:58.380
That's <i>Dix-Neuf</i>'s true form!

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:11.130
Buster Machine #19

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.030
What are you doing, Nono?!
Buster Machine #19

00:21:13.030 --> 00:21:13.230
Buster Machine #19

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:19.060
Embracing pain and suffering, that's just stupid, isn't it?

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.360
But that's what being human is all about!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:28.030
Power isn't based on how big you are, it's based on the strength of your heart!

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:30.760
Isn't that right, Nono?!

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:32.780
That's...

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.660
hard work and guts!!

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:35.770
Yes!

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:48.760
Let's go!

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.380
Right, Onee-sama!

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.020
LIGHTNING...

00:22:00.230 --> 00:22:02.520
DOUBLE...

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:13.730
KICK!!!

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:45.350
Destruction of the fluctuating gravity well confirmed!

00:22:45.350 --> 00:22:48.140
The Schwarzschild radius is also falling apart!

00:22:48.690 --> 00:22:51.190
Impossible! The black hole is splitting apart?!

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:54.070
That's something which isn't allowed to happen in this universe.

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:57.330
If this keeps up, the singularity will become a naked one.

00:22:58.210 --> 00:22:59.330
My God...

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.140
You mean a second Big Bang will happen?!

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:12.690
What on Earth is...

00:23:13.290 --> 00:23:14.810
Impossible to observe.

00:23:15.250 --> 00:23:20.240
Singularities break every single law and equation we know.

00:23:20.240 --> 00:23:22.970
They're a realm in which our physics hold no meaning.

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:42.830
Multi-dimensional Space, Space-Time Censor Room

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:46.960
It's raining outside the window.

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:50.420
It's because I bring rain wherever I go, you say.

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:53.090
It can't be helped...

00:23:53.090 --> 00:23:57.140
so I eat the panini sandwich your mother cooked in the house.

00:23:58.050 --> 00:23:59.870
Begging you repeatedly...

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:03.190
until you relent and let me look at an album of old photos from when you were a kid...

00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:05.770
Teasing the cat and being scratched by it...

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:09.440
During then, when the rain lets up...

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:11.440
Onee-sama, you say...

00:24:12.350 --> 00:24:15.440
"Come on, let's go see some skylarks."

00:24:16.980 --> 00:24:18.490
I open the door...

00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:21.160
and head out under the blue sky.

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:28.400
That's right. I was looking forward to our promise.

00:24:28.740 --> 00:24:30.510
Why are you smiling?

00:24:32.610 --> 00:24:36.490
As long as you never give up on them, wishes always eventually come true.

00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:40.050
We have plenty of time, so...

00:24:40.230 --> 00:24:43.010
You wanted to become an ordinary girl, didn't you?

00:24:43.760 --> 00:24:47.140
I, Nono, will take the singularity that Nono-Riri made shine.

00:24:47.140 --> 00:24:48.730
I won't let you be alone any more!

00:24:48.730 --> 00:24:49.810
In exchange...

00:24:49.810 --> 00:24:52.030
No! Nono! Don't go!

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:02.730
I, Nono, will give you my own singularity, Onee-sama.

00:25:03.300 --> 00:25:04.240
That's because!

00:25:39.680 --> 00:25:41.880
Lal'C, Lal'C!

00:25:42.890 --> 00:25:44.000
Can you hear me?

00:25:46.070 --> 00:25:47.120
Lal'C!

00:25:48.400 --> 00:25:50.760
If you're alive, that's all that matters!

00:25:51.490 --> 00:25:54.380
You could be so much happier without your Topless ability!

00:25:57.630 --> 00:25:58.900
No, that's not it...

00:26:00.040 --> 00:26:03.420
I was able to meet her thanks to that.

00:26:14.860 --> 00:26:21.280
Ten Years Later

00:26:21.330 --> 00:26:25.700
Earth

00:26:25.900 --> 00:26:28.600
Yeah, I've been doing field research.

00:26:28.940 --> 00:26:32.240
The Okinawa Rail... a protected species.

00:26:32.650 --> 00:26:35.540
And you? ...Pluto?

00:26:35.860 --> 00:26:38.880
I'll be protecting a diplomatic envoy as far as Sirius.

00:26:39.240 --> 00:26:43.080
Doesn't the Earth have a lot of festivities going on today for the Star Festival?

00:26:43.410 --> 00:26:47.470
Well, neither of us are at the age where people make wishes any more...

00:26:47.930 --> 00:26:49.670
Didn't you know?

00:26:49.670 --> 00:26:53.190
Last night, the Hawaii Gravitational Observatory confirmed it.

00:27:00.390 --> 00:27:03.820
I don't think I've ever seen a god.

00:27:05.240 --> 00:27:08.330
If a god had something to wish for...

00:27:08.630 --> 00:27:11.060
...what would it pray to?

00:27:12.850 --> 00:27:15.010
I've been waiting a long time for this night.

00:27:15.770 --> 00:27:18.140
I'm really eager to meet with her and tell her...

00:27:18.870 --> 00:27:21.990
about you, the one always smiling...

00:27:35.470 --> 00:27:36.560
That's because!

00:28:05.390 --> 00:28:06.550
That's because...

00:28:06.880 --> 00:28:11.710
the legendary girl you so idolized, Nono-Riri...

00:28:11.710 --> 00:28:13.890
is returning tonight.

00:28:17.480 --> 00:28:21.110
That night, Buster Machines #1 and #2 returned, along with their pilots.

00:28:21.200 --> 00:28:24.530
<b>K
WELCOME BACK</b>

00:31:12.490 --> 00:31:17.500
The End
